                <pb facs="0242" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.248/357: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-20T10:00:00+01:00">May 20, 1940—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 20—7:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>759. For the President. Please give me answers at the earliest possible moment on
                    following questions in previous telegrams: (1) 54 PB Navy bombers; (2) Mackenzie
                    King—reserve pilots to Canada; (3) 2,000 French 75’s; (4) destroyers; (5)
                    Reynaud’s communication which was made orally to me instead of by written
                    note.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
